## 🧩 Services

### 🔐 Auth Service
Manages attorney, paralegal, client, and admin registration, login, role assignment, JWT token issuance, and refresh token rotation. Controls who can see and act on what within the platform.
- 🗄️ **Database:** PostgreSQL (via EF Core) + Redis (session & token cache)
- 🌐 **Port:** `5001`
- 🔑 **Responsibilities:** Register · Login · Refresh Token · RBAC · MFA Support

---

### ⚖️ Case Service
The core of the platform. Manages the full case lifecycle — intake, attorney assignment, conflict-of-interest triggering, status transitions (Open → Active → Pending → Closed → Archived), and case metadata.
- 🗄️ **Database:** PostgreSQL (via EF Core)
- 🌐 **Port:** `5002`
- 🔑 **Responsibilities:** Case CRUD · Attorney Assignment · Status Transitions · Conflict Trigger · Case Search

---

### 📄 Document Service
Manages secure upload, versioning, and retrieval of legal documents. Integrates with **DocuSign** to send envelopes for e-signature, track signature status via webhooks, and store signed copies back to the case record.
- 🗄️ **Database:** MongoDB (document metadata) + Object Storage (file binaries)
- 🌐 **Port:** `5003`
- 🔑 **Responsibilities:** Upload · Versioning · DocuSign Send · Signature Tracking · Webhook Processing · Secure Download

---

### 🏛️ Court Schedule Service
Manages court hearing dates, deadlines, and docket entries. Syncs with external **Court APIs** (PACER / state-level) to pull filing deadlines and hearing schedules. Sends deadline reminders via Kafka events.
- 🗄️ **Database:** PostgreSQL (via EF Core)
- 🌐 **Port:** `5004`
- 🔑 **Responsibilities:** Hearing CRUD · Court API Sync · Deadline Tracking · Calendar Export (iCal) · Reminder Events

---

### 🔍 Conflict of Interest Service
Performs automated conflict-of-interest checks by comparing new client intake data and opposing party information against all existing clients, cases, and attorney relationships. Results are cached in Redis for fast repeated lookups.
- 🗄️ **Database:** PostgreSQL (via EF Core) + Redis (conflict result cache)
- 🌐 **Port:** `5005`
- 🔑 **Responsibilities:** Conflict Check · Opposing Party Matching · Relationship Graph · Cache Invalidation · Audit Logging

---

### 💬 Communication Service
Provides secure, encrypted message threads between attorneys and clients, tied directly to case records. All communications are stored and surfaced in a case timeline. Supports file attachments within threads.
- 🗄️ **Database:** MongoDB
- 🌐 **Port:** `5006`
- 🔑 **Responsibilities:** Message Threads · Secure Messaging · File Attachments · Read Receipts · Case Timeline

---

### 💰 Billing Service
Captures billable time entries (start/stop timer or manual entry), generates itemized invoices, and processes attorney fee payments through **Stripe**. Supports hourly, flat-fee, and contingency billing models with full refund management.
- 🗄️ **Database:** PostgreSQL (via EF Core)
- 🌐 **Port:** `5007`
- 🔑 **Responsibilities:** Time Entry · Invoice Generation · Stripe Charges · Refunds · Trust Account Tracking · Billing Reports

---

### 📩 Notification Service
Consumes Kafka domain events and dispatches email, SMS, and in-app notifications — court deadline reminders, document signature requests, invoice receipts, new message alerts, and case status changes.
- 🗄️ **Database:** MySQL (via EF Core)
- 🌐 **Port:** `5008`
- 🔑 **Responsibilities:** Email · SMS · In-App Alerts · Event Consumption · Notification Preferences · Delivery Tracking

---

### 📋 Audit Log Service
Consumes all domain events from Kafka and writes an **immutable, tamper-evident audit trail** of every action across the platform — required for legal compliance, malpractice defence, and bar association audits.
- 🗄️ **Database:** MongoDB (append-only collection)
- 🌐 **Port:** `5009`
- 🔑 **Responsibilities:** Event Consumption · Immutable Log · Compliance Reporting · Tamper Detection · Log Export

---

## 🔗 Third-Party Integrations

### ✍️ DocuSign eSignature
Embedded in the **Document Service** to send signature envelopes, track signer status in real time via webhooks, and automatically store completed documents back to the case record.

```
Attorney uploads doc → Document Service → DocuSign API (send envelope)
                                        ← DocuSign Webhook (signed/declined)
                                        → Store signed copy → Notify via Kafka
```

### 🏛️ Court APIs (PACER / State Courts)
Integrated into the **Court Schedule Service** to pull docket entries, hearing dates, and filing deadlines directly from court systems, keeping case calendars automatically in sync.

```
Scheduled sync job → Court API → Parse docket entries
                               → Create/update hearings in DB
                               → Emit DeadlineApproaching events → Kafka
```

### 🔍 Conflict-of-Interest Engine
Built into the **Conflict Check Service** using a relationship graph stored in PostgreSQL and cached in Redis. Checks run automatically at case intake and are re-triggered on opposing party changes.

```
New case intake → Case Service → Kafka (CaseIntakeInitiated)
               → Conflict Check Service → Graph query + Redis cache
               → ConflictFound / ConflictClear event → Kafka → Notify attorney
```

