## 🧪 Running Tests

Each service contains three test suites — **Unit**, **Integration**, and **Functional** — following the standard testing pyramid.

```bash
# ── Run ALL tests in a service ──────────────────────────────────────
cd case_service
dotnet test

# ── Unit tests only ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
dotnet test tests/case_service.UnitTests

# ── Integration tests only (requires Docker) ────────────────────────
dotnet test tests/case_service.IntegrationTests

# ── Functional / end-to-end tests (requires Docker) ─────────────────
dotnet test tests/case_service.FunctionalTests

# ── With code coverage report ───────────────────────────────────────
dotnet test --collect:"XPlat Code Coverage"

# ── Run tests across all services from repo root ────────────────────
Get-ChildItem -Recurse -Filter "*.sln" | ForEach-Object {
    dotnet test $_.FullName
}
```

> 💡 **Testcontainers** is used for Integration and Functional tests — it spins up real PostgreSQL, MongoDB, MySQL, and Redis containers automatically. Docker must be running.

