## 🔐 Security & Compliance

Legal platforms handle highly sensitive data. The following security measures are enforced across all services:

### 🛡️ Authentication & Authorisation
- 🔑 **JWT Bearer tokens** with short expiry and **refresh token rotation**
- 👥 **Role-Based Access Control** — Client · Paralegal · Associate · Partner · Admin
- 🔒 **Resource-level authorisation** — attorneys can only access cases assigned to them

### 🔏 Data Protection
- 🔐 **AES-256 encryption** for all client communications and sensitive documents at rest
- 🌐 **TLS 1.3** enforced on all service-to-service and client-to-gateway communication
- 🧂 **Bcrypt password hashing** with per-user salts via ASP.NET Core Identity

### 📋 Audit & Compliance
- 📝 **Immutable audit trail** via the Audit Log Service — every create, update, delete is logged
- 🔍 **Conflict-of-interest checks** run automatically at case intake — results are logged permanently
- 📊 **Structured correlated logging** with Serilog — trace IDs span all services per request

### ⚠️ Secrets Management
- ❌ **No secrets in source control** — enforce via `.gitignore` and pre-commit hooks
- ✅ **Environment variables** or a secrets manager (Azure Key Vault / AWS Secrets Manager) in production
- 🔄 **Stripe webhook signature validation** on every inbound webhook call
- ✍️ **DocuSign HMAC validation** on every inbound DocuSign webhook

