## 🤝 Contributing

### 💛 Welcome, Contributor!

Thank you for your interest in contributing to the **Legal Case Management Platform**! 🎉
Whether you're a .NET veteran, a database specialist, an integration expert, or a first-time open-source contributor — **every contribution matters and you are welcome here**. 🙌

---

### 🧭 Step-by-Step Contribution Guide

#### **Step 1 — 🍴 Fork the Repository**
Click the **Fork** button at the top right of this page to create your personal copy.

#### **Step 2 — 📥 Clone Your Fork**

```bash
git clone https://github.com/asohyannick/legal_case_management.git
cd legal_case_management
```

#### **Step 3 — 🌿 Create a Feature Branch**

```bash
# ✨ New feature
git checkout -b feat/add-docusign-bulk-send

# 🐛 Bug fix
git checkout -b fix/conflict-check-cache-invalidation

# 📖 Documentation
git checkout -b docs/update-billing-service-env-vars

# ♻️  Refactoring
git checkout -b refactor/case-service-clean-architecture

# 🧪 Tests
git checkout -b test/add-audit-log-integration-tests
```

#### **Step 4 — 💻 Make Your Changes**

- ✅ Follow the existing code style enforced by `.editorconfig`
- ✅ Add or update **unit tests** for any logic introduced or modified
- ✅ Run `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` locally before pushing
- ✅ Keep commits small, atomic, and focused — one logical change per commit
- ✅ For integrations (DocuSign, Stripe, Court APIs) — mock external calls in tests

#### **Step 5 — 📝 Commit with a Clear Message**

We follow the [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) specification:

```bash
# ✨ Features
git commit -m "feat(document): add DocuSign bulk envelope send support"
git commit -m "feat(billing): implement contingency fee billing model"
git commit -m "feat(conflict): add opposing counsel relationship check"

# 🐛 Bug fixes
git commit -m "fix(court): correct PACER API date parsing for UTC offsets"
git commit -m "fix(billing): handle Stripe invoice voiding on case dismissal"

# 📖 Documentation
git commit -m "docs(readme): add conflict-of-interest integration flow diagram"

# 🧪 Tests
git commit -m "test(case): add unit tests for case status transition rules"

# ♻️  Refactoring
git commit -m "refactor(audit): migrate to append-only MongoDB collection pattern"
```

#### **Step 6 — 🚀 Push & Open a Pull Request**

```bash
git push origin feat/add-docusign-bulk-send
```

Open a **Pull Request** against `master` and include:
- 📝 **What** you changed and **why**
- 🧪 **How** it was tested (unit / integration / manual)
- 🔗 **Linked issue** (e.g. `Closes #17`)
- 📸 **Screenshots or logs** for behaviour changes
- ⚠️ **Breaking changes** clearly flagged if any

---

### 🔍 What to Work On

Head to the [Issues](https://github.com/asohyannick/legal_case_management/issues) tab:

| 🏷️ Label | 📄 Meaning |
|---|---|
| 🐛 `bug` | Something is broken and needs fixing |
| ✨ `enhancement` | A new feature or meaningful improvement |
| 📖 `documentation` | Docs are missing, outdated, or unclear |
| 🧪 `tests` | Test coverage is missing or incomplete |
| 🔐 `security` | Security hardening or vulnerability fix |
| 🟢 `good first issue` | Perfect for new contributors |
| 🆘 `help wanted` | We'd especially love community input here |
| ⚖️ `compliance` | Legal/regulatory compliance improvements |

---

### 🧑‍💻 Development Guidelines

#### ✅ Architecture Rules
- 🏗️ **Clean Architecture layers must be respected** — no infrastructure or framework dependencies inside `Core` or `UseCases`
- ⚡ **CQRS via MediatR** — all business logic lives in Command/Query Handlers, never in controllers
- 🏷️ **Strongly-typed IDs** — use Vogen value objects for all entity identifiers
- 📤 **Outbox pattern** for all Kafka event publishing — guarantees at-least-once delivery

#### ✅ Integration Rules
- 🔌 **DocuSign, Stripe, and Court API calls** must go through an interface — always mockable in tests
- ⚡ **Redis** is cache-only — it is never the system of record; PostgreSQL/MongoDB is
- 🔐 **All webhook endpoints** must validate signatures before processing any payload

#### ✅ Code Quality
- 🧪 **Unit test every use case handler** — no exceptions
- 🔗 **Integration tests for every repository** using Testcontainers
- ✅ **FluentValidation** for all incoming request models
- 📊 **Serilog structured logging** with correlation IDs — no `Console.WriteLine`
- ⚡ **`async`/`await` everywhere** — zero blocking calls (`.Result`, `.Wait()`)

#### ❌ Hard Rules — Never Do These
- ❌ Do not push directly to `master`
- ❌ Do not commit secrets, API keys, or connection strings
- ❌ Do not add business logic to controllers or API endpoint classes
- ❌ Do not reference `Infrastructure` from `Core` or `UseCases`
- ❌ Do not skip conflict-of-interest checks on case intake endpoints

---

### 🔄 Pull Request Review Process

```
Your PR → 🤖 CI (build + lint + tests) → 👀 Code Review → ✅ Approval → 🔀 Squash Merge
```

- ⏳ A maintainer will review within **3–5 business days**
- 🤖 All CI checks **must pass** — build, test, and code style
- 👥 **At least one approval** required before merging
- 🔀 **Squash-and-merge** preferred to keep history clean

